SSM/GitHub-Actions are overwritten.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/identity.md L88-90: 'Every subsequent identity key add|revoke must be signed by a currently-valid key of that identity ... An unsigned non-genesis change is refused.'","src/rebar/_commands/identity.py `_do_key`/`_load_signature`: add calls `add_identity_key(ns.id, ns.public_key, signature=signature, ...)` where signature comes from --signature-file; 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d already has keys (ticket 7744 shows authorship signed:2), so it is NOT a genesis add.","Plan text only says 'add the new public key to the Rebar Bot identity ... using rebar identity key add' with no --signature-file / DSSE step and no old-key ordering."],"finding":"Item 4's `rebar identity key add` on the existing-keyed Rebar Bot identity 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d is a non-genesis key rotation that MUST be signed by a currently-valid old key (DSSE `--signature-file` over the KEY_ADD op-payload); the plan omits producing that signature and imposes no ordering keeping the old private key available at add time, so the add will be refused.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7e68a358c1a53ba9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope for this task, item 4 (`/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`)","norm_id":"n4897677b1d375a64","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator overwrites SSM and GitHub Actions REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY with the new key first, then runs `identity key add` and the old private key needed to sign the KEY_ADD is no longer at hand.","`identity key add` run without --signature-file → refused as an unsigned non-genesis change."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reorder item 4 to: (1) generate the new keypair; (2) while the old private key is still in hand, sign the KEY_ADD op-payload and run `rebar identity key add 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d '<new-pubkey>' --signature-file <envelope>`; (3) only then overwrite SSM and update GitHub Actions REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the item-4/item-5 completion explicitly gated on the resolution (or a documented workaround) of the P1 Gerrit review-upload rejection (7744 deserved-rubidium-pussycat), since both require merging a change through the Gerrit path; state what to do if that path is blocked (defer the merge-dependent step, keep old key authoritative).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py L2-9 + .rebar/trusted_environments.yaml header: the trusted-env config lives on the CODE branch, 'Gerrit-gated + CODEOWNERS-protected' — editing it produces a change that must pass Gerrit review to take effect.","infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md: `main` advances only through the Gerrit gate (LLM-Review + Verified); GitHub is a read-only mirror.","Ticket 7744 (deserved-rubidium-pussycat) is an OPEN P1: 'Gerrit rejects a valid review upload ... remote unpack failed: error Missing tree ...' blocking `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`.","Plan Safety/sequencing scopes the P1 coordination to 'before any redeploy/restart that could affect Gerrit', not to the fact that item 5 (and item 4's identity event) must traverse the same review/merge path."],"finding":"Items 4 and 5 require landing changes through the Gerrit review path, but the open P1 deserved-rubidium-pussycat (7744) is that Gerrit REJECTS refs/for/main review uploads (missing-tree); the plan only says to 'inspect' that ticket before Gerrit-affecting redeploys and never reckons that the item-5 trusted-env change cannot merge while uploads are blocked.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc0ac20c83764e11d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Safety / sequencing ('inspect deserved-rubidium-pussycat …') and item 5 ('rebar trusted-env add … in a separate worktree/change')","norm_id":"n890f3007388784b2","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator generates the opcert keypair, writes SSM, then tries to land the `trusted-env add` change through Gerrit while refs/for/main uploads are still failing — the new public key never becomes trusted.","Item 4's identity KEY_ADD event and item 5's YAML change stack behind the unresolved P1 upload failure."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sequencing precondition: verify a normal `HEAD:refs/for/main` upload succeeds (per ticket 7744's AC) before attempting the item-5 trusted-env change and the item-4 identity KEY_ADD; if the Gerrit review path is still blocked, defer those merge-dependent steps and keep the old public keys authoritative rather than leaving a live new SSM key with an unmerged public counterpart.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_a